{
  "id": "konjugation",
  "name": "Key irregular verbs in the present",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "it-IT",
  "subtitle": "The most useful Italian verbs do not follow the rules: andare, fare, stare, venire, dare, uscire, dire, bere, sapere. Learn them whole: vado, faccio, sto, vengo, esco, dico, so.",
  "briefMarks": ["andare", "fare", "stare", "venire", "uscire", "sapere"],
  "lookup": { "href": "/present-regular", "label": "Regular verbs first? Present tense: -are, -ere, -ire" },
  "source": "icanspeak Italian original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-12)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "io", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "vado · faccio · sto · vengo · esco · so", "variant": "verb" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-verb\">Vado</span> al lavoro. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Faccio</span> la spesa. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Sto</span> bene. · <span class=\"vp-verb\">Vengo</span> dal Senegal. · Non <span class=\"vp-verb\">so</span>.",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>andare, fare, stare, dare</strong> look alike in many forms: <em>vado, vai, va… vanno</em> / <em>faccio, fai, fa… fanno</em> / <em>sto, stai, sta… stanno</em> / <em>do, dai, dà… danno</em>. The <em>noi</em> and <em>voi</em> forms are almost regular: <em>andiamo, andate</em>.",
        "tag": "-a verbs"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>venire</strong> and <strong>uscire</strong> change the stem in io, tu, lui/lei and loro: <em>vengo, vieni, viene, vengono</em>; <em>esco, esci, esce, escono</em>. With noi and voi they are regular: <em>veniamo, venite; usciamo, uscite</em>.",
        "tag": "venire, uscire"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>dire</strong> and <strong>bere</strong> use an old, longer stem: <em>dire → dic-: dico, dici, dice, diciamo, dite, dicono</em>; <em>bere → bev-: bevo, bevi, beve, beviamo, bevete, bevono</em>.",
        "tag": "dire, bere"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>sapere</strong> = to know a fact or how to do something: <em>so, sai, sa, sappiamo, sapete, sanno</em>. <em>Non lo so.</em> (I don't know.) <em>Sai dov'è la Questura?</em>",
        "tag": "sapere"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>andare a</strong> + town, <strong>andare in</strong> + country or many places: <em>Vado a Roma. Vado in Italia, in banca, in farmacia.</em> <strong>venire da</strong> says where you come from: <em>Vengo da Lagos. Vengo dal lavoro.</em>",
        "tag": "andare, venire"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Io ando</em> → ✓ <em>Io vado</em>. ✗ <em>Io fo, io faco</em> → ✓ <em>Io faccio</em>. ✗ <em>Io sapo</em> → ✓ <em>Io so</em>. ✗ <em>Lui da</em> → ✓ <em>Lui dà</em> (with an accent; <em>da</em> = from). Next: <a href=\"/essere-avere\">Essere and avere</a> and <a href=\"/essere-stare-basics\">Essere or stare</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
